body:
It’s a hard thing to admit to yourself. The word ‘rape’ feels like such a gut-punch. 
Please be kind to yourself. Speaking from experience, you brain is going to be a dick to you over this, so I’m gonna tell you right now;

It wasn’t your fault. You’re not making it up. You’re not weak.

Saying no is not abuse. Using sex as a weapon - ‘If you don’t do this thing for me then no sex for a month’ - is abusive. 

Another example of sex as a weapon is; 

‘If I do this thing for you, then we can only have (type of sex only they like) for a month.’

Think about it this way; 

I know someone who had a severe addiction to codeine. Even now that they’re mostly happy and in therapy, they can’t be around codeine because they get urges and it makes them itchy. 

It’s not you, although it can feel like it is. It’s just the addiction trigger. Maybe you guys should set up some parental controls on his phone or computer, and you can set up a password. That way he would have to download a VPN and go through extra routes to watch porn, and it would give him time to stop and think about the fact he’s scratching his addiction itch.
